I know these may be old news to some, but here goes:
How to defeat shopkeepers:
With a pet, step in the doorway, with the pet already inside the shop.  You
can pick up anything which your pet drops just inside the door, and not have
to pay.  Also, if your pet picks up something good, leave, and walk away
from the shop.  With luck, your pet will follow, carrrying the thing, and
will eventually drop it.  It is possible to clean out magic shops this way,
and if you get things you really don't need, sell them back to the shop-
keeper!!!

Or, if you have a wand of polymorphing:
Poly your pet once or twice, until you get something really kick ass,
like, oh, a Guardian Naga or a Dragon.  Then go into the shop, with your pet
before you.   Wait until you have a direct line of fire on the shopkeeper,
then poly the shopkeeper. I did this and he was turned into a wolf, he
zapped me with a wand once, then my pet Guardian Naga killed him the next
turn.  When you enter the shop, you get the message that it appears
abandoned.  No Keystone Kops!!! Heh!



